# PROPOSED one-off check, NOT installed. Run it ONLY AFTER main is protected and the new poster files are in place
# (checklist step 6). It proves on real GitHub, with protection ON, that the workflow token can claim, record and
# re-read a post on a side branch. It posts nothing and never touches `poster-state` (it uses `poster-state-test`).
#
# Why it exists: a dry run of the poster (mode dry_run) exits before the claim and the save, so it does NOT exercise
# any push. Only this check does. Whether the Actions token is allowed to push a side branch while main is protected
# is not something this review could confirm from GitHub's pages (K-sec-0005, K-sec-0006); this answers it.
#
# Add it, run it once from the Actions tab, read the result, then delete the workflow file and the branch
# `poster-state-test` by hand. If it fails, turn main protection off (checklist rollback) and tell Chief of Staff.
name: Test side-branch gate
on: workflow_dispatch
permissions:
  contents: write
jobs:
  try:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    env:
      STATE_BRANCH: poster-state-test
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Create the throwaway branch (no force)
        run: |
          git config user.name github-actions
          git config user.email github-actions@users.noreply.github.com
          git checkout -q -b "$STATE_BRANCH"
          git push -q origin "HEAD:refs/heads/$STATE_BRANCH"
          git checkout -q -
      - name: Claim, record, and re-read a fake day
        run: |
          set -e
          python3 -B scripts/poster_gate.py restore
          test "$(python3 -B scripts/poster_gate.py claim 2099-01-01 probe)" = claimed
          python3 -B scripts/poster_gate.py complete 2099-01-01 probe-id https://example.invalid/probe
          test "$(python3 -B scripts/poster_gate.py claim 2099-01-01 probe2)" = already-posted
          echo "Gate works on real GitHub with protection on. Delete branch $STATE_BRANCH and this workflow."
